From f23c2356c70a825c177aa3bed6cb9215df335c0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James <james@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:32:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] SuperSprite card: TMS9918A VDP mixed over the Apple
 video, AY-3-8912

A Synetix SuperSprite for any slot (its software expects slot 7):
'Slot 7 = SuperSprite'. Register map from the owner's manual as MAME's
ssprite device has it: VDP at $C0n0/$C0n1, video switches at $C0n3-6,
AY data at $C0nC/D and register select/read at $C0nE/F. The Echo II
TMS5220 is not emulated; its status port reads idle.

- src/apple2/chips/TMS9918A: Graphics I/II, multicolor and text modes,
  32 sprites with 8x8/16x16, magnification, early clock, four per line
  with the fifth-sprite flag, collision, frame interrupt through R1.
- The frame is drawn at each vblank and scaled over the 560x384 Apple
  frame; colour 0 shows the Apple picture (Apple video in on) or black.
- HostInterface gains SetVideoOverlay (appended last), served by a new
  video_set_overlay hook in Video.cpp, called with the frame locked.
- Save states carry VRAM, registers, AY state and the switches.
- tests/test_supersprite.cpp: chip and card tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D6xDKywCB3wTsvh9urrhRo
